  "query_preview": "..\nDeep southwesterly flow remains entrenched across the Marianas this \nafternoon, with visible imagery and Doppler radar showing just\nisolated showers crossing the region. Satellite imagery does show\nsome new convection trying to develop to our southwest, and time\nheights so moistening of the column with increasing omega (lift)\ndeveloping after midnight (more so 2 AM). Thus, will trend the\nforecast in that direction (holding off the better rainfall potential\nuntil later tonight). Otherwise, the inherited forecast remains in\ngood shape with the main changes being to increase rainfall potential\nfor the middle to latter portion of next week, as a tropical \ndisturbance potentially tries to form to our south or southwest.",
